{
 "examples": [
  {
   "name": "Default",
   "summary": "One flexible pane and one sized pane, divided by a handle. Drag the edge, or focus it and use the arrow keys.",
   "sfc": "<script setup>\n  import Resizable from '@aziontech/webkit/resizable'\n  import { ref } from 'vue'\n\n  const basis = ref(240)\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div class=\"h-64\">\n    <Resizable\n      class=\"h-full\"\n      orientation=\"horizontal\"\n      aria-label=\"Workspace\"\n    >\n      <Resizable.Pane aria-label=\"Document\"\n        >Flexible — no basis, so it takes what is left.</Resizable.Pane\n      >\n      <Resizable.Handle aria-label=\"Resize the panel\" />\n      <Resizable.Pane\n        v-model:basis=\"basis\"\n        :min=\"160\"\n        :max=\"480\"\n        aria-label=\"Panel\"\n        >Sized</Resizable.Pane\n      >\n    </Resizable>\n  </div>\n</template>"
  },
  {
   "name": "Orientations",
   "summary": "The axis is this component’s only variant. A horizontal group divides side-by-side panes with a vertical rail; a vertical group stacks them and the rail runs across.",
   "sfc": "<script setup>\n  import Resizable from '@aziontech/webkit/resizable'\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 gap-(--spacing-lg) lg:grid-cols-2\">\n    <div class=\"h-64 overflow-hidden rounded-(--shape-card) border border-(--border-default)\">\n      <Resizable\n        orientation=\"horizontal\"\n        aria-label=\"Side by side\"\n        class=\"h-full\"\n      >\n        <Resizable.Pane aria-label=\"Editor\">Editor</Resizable.Pane>\n        <Resizable.Handle aria-label=\"Resize the preview\" />\n        <Resizable.Pane\n          :basis=\"200\"\n          :min=\"120\"\n          :max=\"400\"\n          aria-label=\"Preview\"\n          >Preview</Resizable.Pane\n        >\n      </Resizable>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"h-64 overflow-hidden rounded-(--shape-card) border border-(--border-default)\">\n      <Resizable\n        orientation=\"vertical\"\n        aria-label=\"Stacked\"\n        class=\"h-full\"\n      >\n        <Resizable.Pane aria-label=\"Editor\">Editor</Resizable.Pane>\n        <Resizable.Handle aria-label=\"Resize the terminal\" />\n        <Resizable.Pane\n          :basis=\"96\"\n          :min=\"48\"\n          :max=\"200\"\n          aria-label=\"Terminal\"\n          >Terminal</Resizable.Pane\n        >\n      </Resizable>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>"
  },
  {
   "name": "Collapsed",
   "summary": "A collapsible pane renders at zero length and stays mounted, so its content keeps its state. The control that brings it back lives OUTSIDE it — a control that only exists inside the thing it hides cannot reopen it.",
   "sfc": "<script setup>\n  import Resizable from '@aziontech/webkit/resizable'\n  import { ref } from 'vue'\n\n  const collapsed = ref(true)\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div class=\"flex flex-col gap-(--spacing-sm)\">\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      @click=\"collapsed = !collapsed\"\n    >\n      {{ collapsed ? 'Show' : 'Hide' }} the preview\n    </button>\n    <div class=\"h-64\">\n      <Resizable\n        class=\"h-full\"\n        aria-label=\"Workspace\"\n      >\n        <Resizable.Pane aria-label=\"Editor\">Editor</Resizable.Pane>\n        <Resizable.Handle aria-label=\"Resize the preview\" />\n        <Resizable.Pane\n          v-model:collapsed=\"collapsed\"\n          :basis=\"240\"\n          :min=\"160\"\n          collapsible\n          aria-label=\"Preview\"\n          >Preview</Resizable.Pane\n        >\n      </Resizable>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</template>"
  }
 ]
}
